From: "Ivan T. Ivanov" <iivanov@suse.de>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:23:44 +0200
Subject: kabi: arm64: errata: Keep workaround bits indexes stable
Patch-mainline: Never, kabi work around
References: git-fixes

kernel-source commit [1] missed fact that workaround bit definitions
are accessible to externally build modules via cpus_have_cap().

Move WORKAROUND_BROKEN_AMU_CONSTCNT to WORKAROUND_2457168 place,
which it actually extends. This way externally build modules
which are build with bit old definition will actually check against
correct workaround.

[1] 01ad172c6aee ("arm64: errata: Factor out broken AMU const counter cap")

Reported-by: Brahmajit Das <bdas@suse.de>
Reviewed-by: Petr Pavlu <petr.pavlu@suse.com>
Signed-off-by: Ivan T. Ivanov <iivanov@suse.de>
---
 arch/arm64/tools/cpucaps |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/tools/cpucaps
+++ b/arch/arm64/tools/cpucaps
@@ -74,6 +74,7 @@ WORKAROUND_1902691
 WORKAROUND_2038923
 WORKAROUND_2064142
 WORKAROUND_2077057
+WORKAROUND_BROKEN_AMU_CONSTCNT
 WORKAROUND_2645198
 WORKAROUND_2658417
 WORKAROUND_AMPERE_AC03_CPU_38
@@ -93,7 +94,6 @@ WORKAROUND_REPEAT_TLBI
 WORKAROUND_SPECULATIVE_AT
 WORKAROUND_SPECULATIVE_SSBS
 WORKAROUND_SPECULATIVE_UNPRIV_LOAD
-WORKAROUND_BROKEN_AMU_CONSTCNT
 PLACEHOLDER_0
 PLACEHOLDER_1
